How MintCam is installed from this package
==========================================

The app is plain Python and uses PySide6, opencv-python, numpy, pyzbar and
Pillow. None of the Python bindings it needs are packaged in Ubuntu the way the
app uses them (PySide6 in particular is split into many small packages), so
instead of shipping a large vendored tree the package installs the app to
/usr/share/mintcam and the /usr/bin/mintcam wrapper creates a per-user virtual
environment in ~/.local/share/mintcam/.venv on first start, installing the
Python requirements from the requirements.txt shipped in the package.

Why this way: it keeps the binary package small (about half a megabyte), works
on every series without rebuilding wheels per Python version, and the
virtualenv is per user so nothing runs as root. The trade-off is that the first
run needs network access and takes a minute or two.

The system dependencies that are actually needed at runtime are declared in
the Depends field: v4l-utils (webcam devices), ffmpeg (audio capture), and
python3-venv/python3-pip for the virtualenv. Everything else comes from the
shipped requirements.txt.
